---
/**
 * Wholesale pricing.
 *
 * The custom and wholesale query cluster — `custom kraft boxes`,
 * `kraft boxes wholesale`, `wholesale kraft paper boxes` — is ~1,867
 * impressions at around position 44 with effectively no clicks. Every
 * competitor ranking above it publishes a visible price signal; this page
 * published none.
 *
 * The figures here are the ones the business already stands behind, read from
 * business-facts.ts rather than restated: a 100-unit minimum and a $0.30
 * starting piece price on qualifying volume. The qualification is not
 * decoration — it is what keeps the claim true, and Product schema's
 * AggregateOffer lowPrice points at this visible text.
 */
import { ORDERING } from '../../data/business-facts'
---

<section class="section section--alt pricing" aria-labelledby="pricing-heading">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section__head" data-reveal>
      <h2 id="pricing-heading">Wholesale kraft box pricing</h2>
      <p>
        Prices can start from {ORDERING.startPrice} per piece on qualifying
        high-volume orders. What your own run costs depends on the
        specification, so here is what actually moves the number.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="pricing__body" data-reveal>
      <p>
        A quote is built from the dimensions, the structure, the material and
        board thickness, the print method, the number of colors, any finishes,
        whether the box takes an insert, the quantity, and how it has to ship.
        Change any one of those and the per-unit figure moves, which is why we
        price each project rather than publish a list.
      </p>

      <p>
        Quantity is the lever with the largest effect. Setup — the dieline, the
        plates, the make-ready on press — is a fixed cost that is paid once
        whether you order 100 boxes or 10,000. Spread across more units it
        shrinks per box, and that is the whole reason a larger run carries a
        lower piece price.
      </p>

      <p>
        The minimum order is {ORDERING.minimumLabel}, and everything from that
        minimum upward is priced at wholesale. There is no separate retail
        tier and no small-order surcharge — a shorter first run simply carries
        more of the setup cost per box than a repeat run of ten times the size.
      </p>

      <p>
        Reordering does not change the price, but it does change the schedule.
        We hold your dieline, board specification and approved artwork, so a
        repeat run references the same specification and skips most of
        prepress. That makes it faster than a first order rather than cheaper.
      </p>

      <p>
        Send dimensions, quantity and artwork and you get a written figure with
        the board grade, structure and print method stated alongside it,
        usually within one business day. If you are not sure which format you
        need yet, the <a href="/products/">full range of kraft boxes</a> is a
        faster way in than describing it from scratch.
      </p>

      {/* TODO: pricing table — add only after real quantity pricing is confirmed */}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .pricing__body {
    max-width: 72ch;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .pricing__body p {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .pricing__body p:last-of-type {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
</style>
